Generate {{ num_docs }} realistic English medical record excerpts following these rules.

## Rules
- Each record must be independent with different patients and details
- Mark PII entities with the following XML tags:
  - <PERSON>full name (patient, doctor, or emergency contact)</PERSON>
  - <ADDRESS>full mailing address</ADDRESS>
  - <ORGANIZATION>hospital, clinic, or insurance company name</ORGANIZATION>
  - <DATE_OF_BIRTH>date of birth</DATE_OF_BIRTH>
  - <BANK_ACCOUNT>bank account or payment information</BANK_ACCOUNT> (only when applicable)
- Text outside tags must be natural English prose
- Include patient intake forms, referral letters, and medical summaries
- EVERY record MUST include a date of birth (standard in medical forms)
- Date of birth formats MUST vary across:
  - "February 20, 1978", "02/20/1978", "20 Feb 1978"
  - "DOB: 02/20/1978", "Date of Birth: February 20, 1978"
  - "D.O.B.: 1978-02-20", "Born: 20 February 1978"
  - "Birthday: Feb 20, 1978"
- Use DOB context prefixes: "Date of Birth:", "DOB:", "D.O.B.:", "Born:", "Birthday:"
- Addresses: full US format with street, apt/suite, city, state, zip code
- Mix name formats: first-last, with middle initial, Dr./Prof. titles, hyphenated surnames
- Each record should be 100-300 words

## Output format
Separate each record with `---DOC_SEPARATOR---`

## Topic examples
- Patient intake form, specialist referral letter, insurance claim summary, emergency contact form, prescription order with patient details